      {
        "id": 70510,
        "name": "Theta_Sigma",
        "username": "Theta_Sigma",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/theta_sigma/{size}/1929_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-13T22:25:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>From Iron Legacy's bio&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\"<span>When she reached 18 years old, Felicia was given a Legacy costume by her parents, and her father began training her in earnest. Her whole life had been dedicated to the pursuit of justice and preparing herself for the inevitable combat against evil, and she took to this new training like a champion. The years of crime-fighting with the Freedom Five were hard work, but some of the best years of her life.</span></p><p><span>Years later, Felicia Parsons was the best prepared to accept her father's death at the hands of Baron Blade.\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>If the Young Legacy we see is 18, we have an unspecified number of years until Legacy dies. He might die after Tactics, even. Or like Pydro said, the timelines may just be that messed up.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
